---
/**
 * website/src/components/CampaignSteps.astro — how it works (go-to-market plan, Task G2.2;
 * spec §6, section 3).
 *
 * **The three steps are the spec's own three**, in the spec's order and in the spec's words:
 * cheap models do the work, a premium model reviews it, and the caps keep the spend in check.
 * They are the same three on all four pages — the campaign's headline is the variant's, the
 * mechanism is the product's — so this is the one section of a campaign page whose copy is not
 * read from `website/data/landing.yaml`, and it is the section the supporting lines under the
 * four headlines describe: a reader who wants to know what the promise rests on gets it here.
 *
 * **Each step is an item of an ordered list, with its own heading and its own icon.** The list
 * is the order a reader reads them in and the order they happen in; the headings are what a
 * screen reader lists the steps by; and the icons are decoration — each one carries
 * `aria-hidden="true"` — because a step named "Caps keep spend in check" beside a picture of a
 * shield says nothing the heading does not, and a picture announced as a picture would put
 * three unnamed images between the reader and the three steps.
 *
 * **The icons are drawn here, from the palette.** Each is one inline `svg` in `currentColor`
 * on the section's own colour, so no icon font, no image file and no third-party request is
 * added to the page, and nothing is fetched that the build did not produce (F14).
 */
---

<section class="campaign-steps" data-section="how-it-works">
  <h2 class="campaign-steps-title display-md">How it works</h2>
  <ol class="campaign-steps-list">
    <li class="campaign-step">
      <svg class="campaign-step-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <ellipse cx="12" cy="6" rx="7" ry="3" />
        <path d="M5 6v6c0 1.7 3.1 3 7 3s7-1.3 7-3V6" />
        <path d="M5 12v6c0 1.7 3.1 3 7 3s7-1.3 7-3v-6" />
      </svg>
      <h3 class="campaign-step-name">Cheap models do the work</h3>
      <p class="campaign-step-line">Every run drafts on the cheap models, and each call is priced as it is made.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="campaign-step">
      <svg class="campaign-step-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="6" />
        <path d="m15.6 15.6 4.4 4.4" />
      </svg>
      <h3 class="campaign-step-name">A premium model reviews it</h3>
      <p class="campaign-step-line">The review and the fixing rounds go to the model the recipe names, so the policy is the same on every developer's machine.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="campaign-step">
      <svg class="campaign-step-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M12 3.5 19 6v6c0 4.2-2.9 7.4-7 8.5-4.1-1.1-7-4.3-7-8.5V6z" />
        <path d="m9 12 2.2 2.2L15.5 10" />
      </svg>
      <h3 class="campaign-step-name">Caps keep spend in check</h3>
      <p class="campaign-step-line">A run stops at the cap you set, and nothing past it is spent.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<style>
  /* Tokens only (W1.2). The steps stack on a phone — the order is the list's, and a phone reads
     them one at a time — and sit in a row from the wide breakpoint, which is the layout the
     static half of `website/test/landing-pages.mjs` reads; the rendered reading at both widths
     is the owner's check (G2.5). */
  .campaign-steps {
    padding-block: var(--space-xl);
    padding-inline: var(--frame-gutter);
  }

  .campaign-steps-title {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .campaign-steps-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .campaign-step-icon {
    color: var(--accent-on-dark);
  }

  .campaign-step-name {
    margin: var(--space-sm) 0 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .campaign-step-line {
    margin: var(--space-2xs) 0 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    /* The phone's own block: the step's line is set at the body size with a little less air
       under the icon, so three steps and their headings fit the narrow column without the
       section becoming a scroll of its own. */
    .campaign-steps {
      padding-block: var(--space-lg);
    }

    .campaign-step-name {
      margin-block-start: var(--space-xs);
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .campaign-steps {
      padding-block: var(--space-2xl);
    }

    .campaign-steps-list {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
